.truss/out/

# Engine kept aside by `truss upgrade` as a rollback copy, and its staging
# directory — both are engine copies, never project content.
.truss.bak-*/
.truss.incoming/

# OS / editor junk
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Host-agent config. Skills and commands you write are project content — keep
# them tracked so the team gets them. Only the per-machine settings are local.
.claude/settings.local.json
.cursor/settings.local.json

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Capture drives and phone test sets. The images stay inside the repo so the
# project is one directory, but they never enter the history — a single drive
# is hundreds of megabytes.
captures/

# Presentation build output and the viewer asset it inlines. Both are generated
# — `presentation/build.py` rebuilds the deck from the template and the assets,
# and its docstring carries the splat-transform recipe for the viewer. Same
# reasoning as captures/: reproducible bulk does not belong in the history.
presentation/deck.html
presentation/assets/room.html
